From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c <a@b>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 00:14:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: give the Linux runner the Qt runtime libraries

WHAT THIS IS
    The Linux runner of GitHub Actions has no `libEGL.so.1`, so the
    whole desktop test suite stops with an ImportError the moment
    PySide6 is imported. The repository installs that library from its
    own content (`scripts/qt_runtime.py`, called by `conftest.py`), and
    this patch is the explicit, workflow level line of defence.

WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT THE WORKFLOW FILE
    The GitHub App that pushes this repository has no `workflows`
    permission, so it cannot write `.github/workflows/`. This change
    therefore travels as a patch, and the owner applies it once.

    This patch used to add the `fail-fast` setting as well, with the
    very same lines that `patches/github-actions-green.patch` adds, so
    the two could not both be applied. The `fail-fast` setting lives in
    `github-actions-green.patch` alone, and this file carries only the
    runtime libraries, which is what its name says.

---
 .github/workflows/tests.yml | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/tests.yml b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
index 3862b81..7c32599 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/tests.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/tests.yml
@@ -15,5 +15,11 @@ jobs:
       - uses: actions/setup-python@v5
         with:
           python-version: '3.12'
+      - name: Install the Qt runtime libraries
+        if: runner.os == 'Linux'
+        run: |
+          sudo apt-get update
+          sudo apt-get install -y --no-install-recommends \
+            libegl1 libglib2.0-0 libdbus-1-3 libxkbcommon0 libfontconfig1
       - run: python -m pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
       - run: python -m pytest -q
